# P7 · Hospital enterprise and integrations · Weeks 36–60 · R7 Enterprise
# exit: 1 integration contract + security review passed · 2 write-back ≥ 99 % success, every conflict visible · 3 hospital clinical sign-off
# nfr:  1 SIEM export, privileged access review · 2 App Service → AKS when stamp count or isolation requires it
# pkg:  1 integration specification + runbook · 2 security evidence pack
# dep:  1 hospital procurement + HIS vendor cooperation

@epic MDV-P7-E01 | Hospital onboarding and record authority | P7-01, P7-02 | Per-facility authority and multi-facility organisation without a second conflicting chart.
@epic MDV-P7-E02 | Enterprise identity | P7-03 | SSO, SCIM and facility-scoped role grants.
@epic MDV-P7-E03 | Integrations and write-back | P7-04 | FHIR/HL7 interfaces, lab feeds, imaging links and a visible write-back queue.
@epic MDV-P7-E04 | Governance and dedicated deployment | P7-05, P7-06 | Audit, break-glass, retention/residency, data requests, analytics and a dedicated hospital stamp.

=== MDV-P7-001
title: Hospital procurement, HIS vendor engagement and integration contract
type: Chore
epic: MDV-P7-E01
prd: P7-04
covers: dep:1, exit:1, pkg:1
priority: MUST
roles: Founder, Hospital IT
labels: enterprise, contract
estimate: 3
weeks: 36-40
confidence: 40 | Entirely dependent on a hospital customer and its HIS vendor.
sources: PRD v2 P7 dependency 1, exit 1
desc:
Sign the first hospital; agree the integration specification with the HIS vendor (FHIR R4 resources/HL7 messages, auth, environments, error semantics, receipts), security review and runbook.
ac:
- Signed hospital contract and integration specification (delivery package 1).
- Security review by the hospital passed (exit gate 1).

=== MDV-P7-002
title: Hospital onboarding wizard and record authority per facility (H-08)
type: Story
epic: MDV-P7-E01
prd: P7-01
screens: H-08
priority: MUST
roles: Hospital IT
labels: enterprise, authority
estimate: 3
weeks: 40-42
depends: MDV-P7-001
confidence: 78 | Interactive design with mixed-authority warning exists.
sources: design/Medvya Enterprise Pages (H-08); docs/02-design/screen-specs.md#enterprise-p7--medvya-enterprise-admin-medvya-enterprise-pages
desc:
Steps Organisation → Facilities → SSO → HIS connection → Record authority → Pilot go-live. Per facility choose Medvya EMR or Existing HIS; statuses "HIS authoritative · write-back on" / "Medvya authoritative" / "HIS not connected yet"; mixed-authority warning; sets ENCOUNTER.authority_mode.
ac:
- Authority is set per facility and stamped on every new encounter.
- With HIS authority, chart items show "Synced from HIS" and Medvya never creates a second authoritative chart.
- Mixed authority shows the attention banner and cross-facility views show source badges.

=== MDV-P7-003
title: Organisation, facilities and departments administration (H-02)
type: Story
