=== MDV-P7-006
title: FHIR R4 HIS interface and write-back queue with conflict review and retry (H-04)
type: Story
epic: MDV-P7-E03
prd: P7-04
screens: H-04
covers: exit:2
priority: MUST
roles: Hospital IT, Doctor
labels: fhir, write-back, integration
estimate: 8
weeks: 46-52
depends: MDV-P7-005, MDV-P7-002
confidence: 55 | Depends on the specific HIS vendor's FHIR capabilities.
sources: design/Medvya Enterprise Admin (H-04 queue); docs/03-architecture/state-machines.md#integration-delivery-p7
desc:
Firely SDK client; read patient/encounter/meds into "Synced from HIS" copies; write back only clinician-signed content (DocumentReference, MedicationStatement…) with idempotency keys and receipts; queue states Delivered/Failed/Conflict/Retrying/Sent to clinician; conflict diff (Medvya signed v1 vs HIS current) routed to the signing clinician; transport errors retried by IT; chart shows "Not yet in HIS".
ac:
- Medvya never overwrites the HIS silently; conflicts always go to the clinician (test).
- Write-back success ≥ 99 % in the pilot with every failure/conflict visible (exit gate 2).
- Duplicate deliveries are prevented by idempotency keys.
- Attempts list shows timestamps and response codes without PHI in logs.

=== MDV-P7-007
title: Lab feeds (HL7 v2 ORU/ORM over MLLP/VPN) and imaging viewer links (N-15)
type: Story
epic: MDV-P7-E03
prd: P7-04
screens: N-15
priority: MUST
roles: Doctor, Hospital IT
labels: hl7, lab, imaging, design-needed
estimate: 5
weeks: 48-52
depends: MDV-P7-005, MDV-P4-014
confidence: 50 | DESIGN NEEDED for N-15; lab vendor specifics unknown.
sources: PRD v2 P7-04 (N-15); design/Medvya Gap Analysis (external lab and imaging feeds)
desc:
Orders out (ORM^O01) and results in (ORU) with ACK handling; results land in the results inbox with identity match; radiology reports as text with DICOMweb viewer links (no image copies).
ac:
- ORU messages create inbox items matched to orders; low-confidence matches still need a human.
- ACK/NACK handling and retries are visible in H-01.
- Imaging opens in the provider viewer via link only.

=== MDV-P7-008
title: Audit log and break-glass review (H-05)
type: Story
epic: MDV-P7-E04
prd: P7-05
screens: H-05
priority: MUST
roles: Hospital IT, Privacy officer, Doctor
labels: audit, break-glass
estimate: 3
weeks: 50-52
depends: MDV-P0-017
confidence: 80 | Designed; audit foundation exists since P0.
sources: design/Medvya Enterprise Admin (H-05 audit table); docs/02-design/sitemap-and-permissions.md
desc:
Break-glass: temporary read with typed justification, banner, short expiry, post-hoc review queue; audit explorer with filters (actor, patient ref, action, purpose); repeated break-glass alerts the privacy officer.
ac:
- Break-glass requires justification, expires automatically and appears as "Pending review".
- Reviewers record outcomes; repeated use triggers an alert.
- Audit explorer shows opaque patient refs; no PHI in logs.

=== MDV-P7-009
title: Retention and residency policies (H-06) and data subject requests with tamper-evident export (H-10)
type: Story
epic: MDV-P7-E04
prd: P7-05
screens: H-06, H-10
priority: MUST
roles: Privacy officer, Hospital IT
labels: retention, residency, dsr
estimate: 4
weeks: 52-55
depends: MDV-P5-025
confidence: 72 | Designed; legal rules per hospital contract.
sources: design/Medvya Enterprise Pages (H-06, H-10)
desc:
Policy page (region, CMK rotation, audio retention, transcripts, medical records, audit retention, cross-border disabled — labels are configured policy, not certifications); request queue (access, correction, deletion with legal hold, withdraw recording consent with vendor purge receipt), tamper-evident export ZIP.
ac:
- Policies are configurable per hospital tenant and enforced by retention jobs.
- Requests track due dates and outcomes; deletion under legal hold shows "Partially fulfilled · legal hold".
- Exports are tamper-evident (hash manifest) and audited.

